required to be true.\n- A **commitment** is an account's acceptance of a conjecture. Commitment is local to an account. Different accounts may commit to incompatible conjectures.\n- A **refutation** is one of: (a) a counterexample within an account's own viewpoint; (b) a derivation of inconsistency within an account's own reading; or (c) a demonstration that a conjecture depends on an assumption that another account rejects. Refutations are local to accounts and do not force global agreement.\n\n**What RSS permits**\n\nRSS permits the representation of uncertainty without forcing resolution. It permits multiple readings of expiry and release to coexist. It permits criticism to target specific elements. It permits negative availability as a signal. It permits the distinction between exact and near-duplicates. It permits the distinction between a rule criticism and a data criticism. It permits the idea that the snapshot is a merge of replica views, without deciding union, intersection, or single-view.\n\n**What RSS may obstruct**\n\nRSS may obstruct efficient decision-making because it refuses to produce a single answer. It may obstruct comparison between accounts because it lacks a common metric. It may obstruct automation because it is noncomputable and requires human or external choice. It may obstruct reasoning about physical resources because it does not include a resource model unless one is added as a primitive. It may obstruct reasoning about time across replicas because it treats logical time as viewpoint-relative without a mechanism for aligning viewpoints. It may obstruct the very idea of a snapshot as a single object, because it treats a snapshot as one viewpoint among many.\n\n**Unresolved expressive limitations**\n\nRSS cannot express the exact provenance of a delivery unless provenance is added. RSS cannot express physical resource sharing beyond what an account includes. RSS cannot express replica agreement protocols. RSS cannot express the operational